{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conversational Ability.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conversational Ability.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conversational ability conversational ability","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conversational Ability.md","fileName":"Conversational Ability.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conversational Ability","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Virtual Assistant Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Virtual Assistant Architecture","Intent Schema","aiassistants.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conversational Ability.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conversational Ability.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conversational ability conversational ability","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conversational Ability.md","fileName":"Conversational Ability.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conversational Ability","heading":"Conversational Ability","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Conversational ability is a system's capacity to exchange turns in natural language while preserving enough meaning and context to move an interaction forward. It depends on more than recognizing words: the system must interpret intent, manage state, choose actions, and express responses.\n\nConversational fluency is not a reliable measure of general intelligence. A system can produce socially plausible language while having little knowledge or utility beyond a narrow [[Intent Schema]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Virtual Assistant Architecture","Intent Schema","aiassistants.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conversational Ability.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conversational Ability.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__n